================================================================================
CHALLENGE 1: THE "SECURE DATA MASKER" (Strings & Characters)
================================================================================
Context: Protecting Sensitive Personal Information (SPI).
1. Create a class 'DataProcessor'.
2. Method: 'maskCreditCard(String cardNumber)'
3. Logic:
   - Accept a string of 16 digits.
   - Use 'StringBuilder' (for efficiency) to replace the first 12 digits with 'X'.
   - Keep the last 4 digits visible.
   - Requirement: If the input isn't exactly 16 digits, return "Invalid Card".
4. Goal: Demonstrate the difference between 'String' (immutable) and
   'StringBuilder' (mutable).